From: TX68 Build <tx68@local>
Subject: [PATCH] tx68: give an externally loaded FDT room before fixups

With 0002 in place U-Boot finally boots with the DTB the boot script loaded
("Booting using the fdt blob at 0x46000000"), but then dies immediately:

    WARNING: could not set bootargs FDT_ERR_NOSPACE.
    ERROR: /chosen node create failed
     - must RESET the board to recover.

image_setup_libfdt() calls fdt_chosen() to add /chosen bootargs and the initrd
range. Allwinner's tree skips the fdt_shrink_to_minimum() call (guarded by
#ifndef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) that normally page-aligns totalsize upward and thus
creates the slack those fixups need -- their control FDT always lives in a
pre-padded CONFIG_SUNXI_FDT_ADDR region, so it never needed it.

A DTB loaded from disk is exactly its file size (44077 bytes here) with zero
spare room, so fdt_chosen() fails. The existing shrink call cannot help even if
re-enabled: it runs *after* fdt_chosen(), not before.

Grow an externally supplied blob at the very top of image_setup_libfdt, before
any fixup touches it. gd->fdt_blob (the vendor control FDT) is compared by
pointer and left on the original path, so the vendor 5.4 boot flow is unchanged.
---
--- a/common/image-fdt.c
+++ b/common/image-fdt.c
@@ -469,6 +469,43 @@
 	int ret = -EPERM;
 	int fdt_ret;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
+	/*
+	 * Allwinner skips the fdt_shrink_to_minimum() call further down (see the
+	 * CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI guard below) because their control FDT always lives
+	 * in a pre-padded CONFIG_SUNXI_FDT_ADDR region, so it already has room
+	 * to grow. A DTB loaded from disk by a boot script has no such slack --
+	 * it is exactly its file size -- and fdt_chosen() below then fails with
+	 * FDT_ERR_NOSPACE the moment it tries to add /chosen bootargs, hanging
+	 * the board before Linux is ever entered ("could not set bootargs
+	 * FDT_ERR_NOSPACE" / "/chosen node create failed").
+	 *
+	 * Note the shrink call further down cannot fix this: it runs *after*
+	 * fdt_chosen(). Grow an externally supplied blob here instead, before
+	 * any fixup touches it. gd->fdt_blob (the vendor control FDT) is left
+	 * exactly as before.
+	 */
+	if (blob != gd->fdt_blob) {
+		ret = fdt_open_into(blob, blob, of_size + 0x3000);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			printf("ERROR: failed to grow fdt: %s\n",
+			       fdt_strerror(ret));
+			goto err;
+		}
+		/*
+		 * of_size must follow the blob, otherwise the
+		 * "of_size += FDT_RAMDISK_OVERHEAD; fdt_set_totalsize()" below
+		 * would force totalsize back down to the original file size --
+		 * which by then is *smaller* than the content, because
+		 * fdt_chosen() has already appended /chosen and the bootargs
+		 * string. That silently truncates the blob we hand to Linux.
+		 * The generic path keeps of_size in sync via the return value
+		 * of fdt_shrink_to_minimum(); do the equivalent here.
+		 */
+		of_size = fdt_totalsize(blob);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	if (fdt_root(blob) < 0) {
 		printf("ERROR: root node setup failed\n");
 		goto err;
